    <div class="pictochat-message">
        <header class="ds-lime-50">Game Modding</header>
        <span>
            Most of these projects required <b>significant reverse engineering effort</b>, as documentation
            was obviously missing, and using certain language features in the wrong way would cause an
            <i>instant error-less crash</i>. They also required an eye for optimization, as games have a
            tight frametime budget, and in a VR game, lag can <b>cause someone to throw up</b>.
        </span>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://thunderstore.io/c/lethal-company/p/extraes/LethalLoudnessMeter/">LethalLoudnessMeter</a>:
                a simple mod that just shows how loud you're being. It got 700,000+ downloads.
                <br/>- Made in my first year of college.
            </li>

            <li><a href="https://github.com/extraes/SceneSaverBL">SceneSaverBL</a>:
                asynchronous saving & loading of game objects (read: GMod dupes), made with special
                consideration for performance and small filesize, using custom de/serialization routines
                instead of an off-the-shelf format like JSON. This also required
                <a href="https://github.com/BepInEx/Il2CppInterop/pull/133">modifying the proxy code
                    generator</a> to allow mods to interop with the base game's async code.
                <br/>- Made through college, started as a senior in HS.
            </li>


            <li><a href="https://thunderstore.io/c/boneworks/p/extraes/SepticSurvival/">Septic Survival</a>:
